    <string name="rules_title">How to play</string>
    <string name="rules_body">Find the one square in every color where a dog belongs.\n\nTap a square to cross it off. Tap it twice to place a dog there. Cross off freely — only placing a dog can cost you a bone.</string>
    <string name="rules_region_body">Every color holds exactly one dog. Once a dog lands, the rest of that color is out.</string>
    <string name="rules_line_body">Every row and every column holds exactly one dog too.</string>
    <string name="rules_touch_body">No two dogs may touch, not even corner to corner.</string>

    <string name="bones_title">Bones</string>
    <string name="bones_body">Three bones per attempt. Placing a dog on the wrong square costs one. Run out and the attempt ends — but you can watch an ad for three more, or start the puzzle over.\n\nCrossing squares off is always free.</string>

